<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Leo XIII</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1810">1810</a>–<a href="/years/1903">1903</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Vincenzo Gioacchino Pecci</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pope Leo XIII (1810–1903), born Vincenzo Gioacchino Pecci, was head of the Catholic Church from 1878 to 1903. His encyclical Rerum novarum of 1891 laid the foundations of modern Catholic social teaching on labour and capital. He also acted as an international arbitrator, notably in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caroline-islands">Caroline Islands</a> dispute of 1885 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, which he settled in Spain's favour.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-leo-xiii.jpg" alt="Pope Leo XIII" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Braun et Compagnie · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Papa_Leone_XIII_(3x4_cropped).jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Christian trade unions took their lead from <b>Pope Leo XIII</b>’s encyclical Rerum novarum (1891), which defended workers’ right to form associations and to receive a just wage, and the American Federation of Labor kept largely to bargaining over pay and hours.</blockquote><a href="/movement/labour-movement">Labour movement · Aims</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Pope Leo XIII</b> added it to the prayers said at the end of Low Mass; it is traditionally sung at the end of a priest's funeral Mass and said at the end of the Rosary.</blockquote><a href="/songs/salve-regina">Salve Regina</a></li><li><blockquote>A dispute between Spain and Germany over Yap in 1885 was settled by <b>Pope Leo XIII</b> in Spain's favour, and Spanish rule began in 1886.</blockquote><a href="/state/yapese-chiefdoms">Yapese chiefdoms</a></li></ul></section>
